            <div class="fs-label">The Problem</div>
            <h2>Why most drummers struggle with fills and solos</h2>
            <p>Most drummers practice the same few fills over and over until they become habits. When a solo opportunity comes, they default to what they know and run out of ideas fast. The problem is not lack of technique — it is lack of <strong>organized vocabulary</strong>.</p>
            <p>A fill is really just a sticking pattern applied around the kit. A solo is a sequence of fills connected musically. If you have a deep library of sticking patterns you can apply instinctively, your fills and solos become more varied, more musical, and more confident.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

